  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Insulated solid copper rods of different diameters and fixed length are placed in thermal contact with two objects X and Y, maintained at different temperatures T<sub>X</sub>  and T<sub>Y</sub> respectively. The diagram shows the setup with one such rod.</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p>\n<p><br/>Which graph shows the variation with rod diameter d of the rate of thermal energy transfer <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{\\Delta  Q}{\\Delta  t}\"></span> along the rod?</p>\n<p><br/></p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p>\n<p>[1]</p><ol class=\"mcq-options\"><li data-label=\"A\">Option A is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"B\">Option B is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"C\">Option C is shown in the figure above.</li><li data-label=\"D\">Option D is shown in the figure above.</li></ol>"
